
==========================================================================
  ART-3 PROBE: nested phased_omap0 phase support
==========================================================================

  Types:
    X = one + one           (inner sum, 1 tag qubit)
    Y = X + one = (one+one)+one   (nested outer sum, 2 tag qubits total)

  Test term (under audit):
    T = phased_omap0 (-1) X one (id X) (id one) : Y → Y
    Should apply phase -1 whenever outer tag = 0, i.e. at BOTH
    inner-tag values within the left summand.

  Reference (built from orthogonal primitives — no phased_omap0):
    R = omap0 X one (phase (-1) X) (id one) : Y → Y
    `phase (-1) X` multiplies the whole X = one+one summand by -1,
    then `omap0` places this on the outer left branch and id on
    the outer right branch. Semantically the correct diagonal
    diag(-1, -1, 1, ?).

  test_term (phased_omap0 -1 X one id id) — should be 2 phase blocks:
2 qubits, 8 gates
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  CU1 q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  X q[1]
  X q[0]
  CU1 q[0, 1]
  X q[0]
  perm: [0, 1]
    (gate count: 8)

  test_term ; test_term = id  (involution, all phased tags square to 1):
    EQUAL       fidelity=1.000000

  4-th root sanity: phased_omap0 (+i) applied 4 times = id

  test_i^4 = id:
    EQUAL       fidelity=1.000000

  Flat (binary) case sanity: phased_omap0 (-1) squared on Plus(one,one)

  flat_test ; flat_test = id  (binary sum involution):
    EQUAL       fidelity=1.000000

==========================================================================
  ART-4a PROBE: phased_control honors branches argument
==========================================================================

  Under the fix, phased_control compiles as (control ; PhasedCtrl),
  so branches are applied then phases. Verification:
    A = phased_control desc phases q [ id; id; id ]  ← all-id
    B = phased_control desc phases q [ X; H; Z ]     ← nontrivial
  Under the fix, A ≠ B (branches affect the circuit). Pre-fix, A = B.

  A (all-id) vs B (nontrivial)   -- FIX confirms A ≠ B (branches honored):
    NOT EQUAL   fidelity=0.250000

  Sanity: phased_control desc [1;1;1] q [id;id;id] = id

  trivial phased_control = id_{D⊗Q}:
    EQUAL       fidelity=1.000000

==========================================================================
  ART-4b PROBE: phased_control endianness (big-endian, matches NPlusMap)
==========================================================================

  Under the fix, PhasedControl uses _emit_exact_tag_phase — the same
  big-endian helper as NPlusMap. Verification via involution:
    phased_control desc [-1; 1; 1] q [id;id;id] squared = id
  (phasing a single specific tag basis state by -1 twice = 1.)

  phased_control with single -1 phase, squared = id:
    EQUAL       fidelity=1.000000

==========================================================================
  FINDINGS SUMMARY
==========================================================================

  ART-3 (nested phased_omap0):  FIXED.
    Post-fix, test_term emits two exact-tag phase blocks — one for
    each tag value in {0..n_left-1}. Involution square = id at
    fidelity 1.0 verifies the fix; the 4-th-root variant with phase
    +i further sanity-checks by requiring 4 applications = id.
    Fix landed in python/src/compile/to_pytket.py (PhasedPlusMap
    Strategy A: replace all-tag-bits anti-control with a loop over
    range(n_left) calling _emit_exact_tag_phase).

  ART-4a (phased_control ignores branches):  FIXED.
    Post-fix, OCaml phased_control compiles as (control dt a_ty
    branches ; PhasedCtrl), so branches are applied then phases.
    A ≠ B now confirms branches affect the circuit. Trivial
    phased_control (all-id branches, phases-all-1) equals id.
    Fix landed in ocaml/lib/linear.ml.

  ART-4b (tag-index endianness):  FIXED.
    Post-fix, PhasedControl uses the shared _emit_exact_tag_phase
    big-endian helper — same convention as NPlusMap. The involution
    check (single-phase squared = id) verifies the encoding round-
    trips through the correct tag basis state.
    Fix landed in python/src/compile/to_pytket.py (PhasedControl
    handler: replace the little-endian (branch_idx >> bit_pos) with
    a call to _emit_exact_tag_phase).

  All three bugs share the phased-emitter code path and were fixed
  jointly. See docs/LIMITATIONS.md §7 for the historical entry.

==========================================================================
  END OF PROBE
==========================================================================
